Of course, if you take this with the previous sentence (probably 
shouldn't've been a seperate paragraph, I apologize), you realize that 
it makes sense. I was pointing out how nethack can actually be compared 
to real life in this case. Armor is the clothing of NetHack. And yes, 
this may be stating the obvious.

The OP asked if there's a difference between putting things on and 
wearing them in real life. I maintain that although we use the words 
interchangeably, there is at least some fundamental difference in the 
actions (in this case divided into 'clothing' and 'everything else', 
which could further be split).

Personally, I prefer seperate commands for everything. If there were 
enough keys, I'd want one for (for example) dropping all unknown buc 
status items, instead of having to go through 2 menus to do so. I don't 
favor combining the commands unless we need one of those keys for 
something else.

